            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it. Tried a glass first with just a little salt and pepper added. Great. Then I added a shot of vodka. Even better.\nI did use pickling cucumbers so no bitter taste.",
            "datePublished": "2017-09-22T01:31:02.087Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Steve Watt"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Variation: We didn't have lime so added two mint leaves instead. We also don't have a juicer so I peeled the cucumber and threw it all in our high-speed blender. Yum. Would put over ice next time to chill it further.",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-03T14:08:12.860Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dodi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Do not use bitter cucumbers. Taste first. Try small pickling or English cucumbers. \nCostco sells bottles of this when watermelons are in season but theirs has sugar added and I can’t eat sugar and really, with sweet melons, sugar is unnecessary. \n This is great for cooling off on a hot day. I have tried adding alcohol.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-08T03:33:22.780Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Thomas Fogarty"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We added the rind of both the watermelon and the cucumber as well (95% of the vitamins) and a touch of local honey. Good and good for you.",
            "datePublished": "2013-08-10T08:40:17.337Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "1"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Melissa Goff"
            },
            "reviewBody": "What threw me off on this recipe is the amount of watermelon. It states 1/2(4 pound) watermelon, so I measured 4 pounds then used 4 cucumbers. I threw the cucumbers into my juicer 1st and dipped my finger into the juice...shouldn't have done that... I love cucumbers, but never have had it in a juiced form...and I can say, I'll never do that again. It was very bitter. But proceeded on with juicing my watermelon and then mixing it all together in the end with 2 limes. It was not sweet or even slightly sweet, tasted like a very tart cucumbers with lime. I had a couple of bites of my watermelon before juicing and it was totally sweet. The batch made well over 2 liters of juice all together. I added a cup and a quarter of Ideal sweetener (like splenda) to the batch. And even though I could still taste the cucumber it wasn't as tart &amp; was edible or in this case, drinkable; turned them into popsicles. I would cut the cucumber &amp; lime in half OR use 8 pounds of watermelon",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-23T09:04:10.340Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "deathbychocolat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a good recipe. For those who got bitter cucumber juice: remember that sometimes cucumbers can have a bitter skin. Try the cucumber first before juicing it. If the cucumber has a bitter skin, peel the cucumber, then juice it.\nThis juice is very refreshing on a hot summer's day.",
            "datePublished": "2014-05-24T10:14:41.280Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tay Nicole"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is such a refreshing drink!!! I'm not gonna lie, the 2nd time I made this I added a little moonshine to it, and it was still amazing. My new go-to summer drink!!! 10/10 recommend. I added lime zest to the mix.",
